    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14709" root="رتك" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرْتَكٌ</span></b>  <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْدَاسَنْجٌ</span> [from the Pers. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُردَاسَنْگ</span>,
both of which signify <i>Litharge</i> in the present day,
as in the classical dialect]: (K:) it is of two kinds;
namely, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذَهَبِىٌّ</span> [i. e. <i>red,</i> or <i>of gold</i>], and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِضِّىٌّ</span>
[i. e. <i>white,</i> or <i>of silver</i>]. (TA.)

